%S A400910 1,0,48,21000,25154640,63085357440,286897800420000,
%T A400910 2145618583464676320,24594468312668173920000,
%U A400910 409784202420212292645772800,9522425545256642530158059212800,298553697757276058027083137304320000,12291080412430808026883479426549940582400,649556576277852583632749534556957301824000000
%N A400910 Number of labeled loopless digraphs on 2n vertices such that (deg^-(v), deg^+(v)) is either (1,2) or (2,1) for every vertex v.
%C A400910 Here deg^-(v) and deg^+(v) denote the indegree and outdegree of v, respectively.
%C A400910 Exactly n vertices have each of the two degree types.
%C A400910 Equivalently, a(n) counts 2n X 2n binary matrices with zero diagonal such that, for each i, the pair consisting of the i-th row sum and the i-th column sum is either (1,2) or (2,1).
%C A400910 a(n)/binomial(2*n,n) counts 2n X 2n binary matrices with zero diagonal whose first n rows and last n columns sum to 2, while the remaining rows and columns sum to 1.
%H A400910 Vladeta Jovovic, <a href="/A400910/b400910.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..150</a>
%F A400910 a(n) = binomial(2*n,n) * coefficient of (x_1^2*y_1)*...*(x_n^2*y_n)*(x_(n+1)*y_(n+1)^2)*...*(x_(2n)*y_(2n)^2) in Product_{1 <= i,j <= 2n, i != j} (1 + x_i*y_j).
%e A400910 For n = 2, there are 24 tournaments on 4 labeled vertices with no source or sink.
%e A400910 There are also 24 digraphs consisting of two disjoint pairs of oppositely directed arcs and two single arcs joining the pairs: 3 choices for the pairing, 2 choices for the matching between the pairs, and 2^2 orientations.
%e A400910 Thus a(2) = 24 + 3*2*2^2 = 48.
%e A400910 For n = 2, the coefficient of x_1^2*y_1*x_2^2*y_2*x_3*y_3^2*x_4*y_4^2 in
%e A400910 (1 + x_1*y_2)*(1 + x_1*y_3)*(1 + x_1*y_4)*
%e A400910 (1 + x_2*y_1)*(1 + x_2*y_3)*(1 + x_2*y_4)*
%e A400910 (1 + x_3*y_1)*(1 + x_3*y_2)*(1 + x_3*y_4)*
%e A400910 (1 + x_4*y_1)*(1 + x_4*y_2)*(1 + x_4*y_3)
%e A400910 = 1 + x_1*y_2 + x_1*y_3 + x_1*y_4 + x_2*y_1 + ... + 8*x_1^2*x_2^2*x_3*x_4*y_1*y_2*y_3^2*y_4^2 + ...
%e A400910 is 8. Thus a(2) = binomial(4,2)*8 = 48.
%Y A400910 Cf. A400909 (all vertices have total degree 3), A400907 (total degree 2).
